<h1 class="text-2xl font-bold">GitHub - acme-gh</h1>
<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 mt-1">
<span class="text-sm text-gray-500">GitHub organisation acme-gh &middot; connected by octo-owner</span>
<span class="inline-flex items-center px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-medium bg-green-50 text-green-700">Healthy</span>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<form method="POST" action="/orgs/testorg/settings/integrations/ID/delete" data-confirm="Disconnect this GitHub organisation from Forest? Uninstall the app on GitHub too to revoke its access.">
<input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="test-csrf">
<button type="submit" class="px-3 py-1.5 text-sm text-red-600 border border-red-200 rounded-md hover:bg-red-50 transition-colors">Disconnect</button>
</form>
</div>
<h2 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wide mb-3">Attribution coverage</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-3">A release authored on GitHub reaches its author individually only when they linked that GitHub account to their Forest account (signing in with GitHub does this). GitHub membership is shown for context and never grants access to Forest.</p>

